1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:03,300
In the year 845,

2
00:00:03,510 --> 00:00:09,140
the Colossal Titan and the
Armored Titan suddenly appeared

3
00:00:09,350 --> 00:00:14,140
and destroyed one of humanity's walls..
and everyday life with it.

4
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:19,020
Humanity abandoned Wall Maria,

5
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:22,820
lost 20% of its population and
one-third of its territory,

6
00:00:23,030 --> 00:00:27,780
and was forced to retreat behind Wall Rose.

7
00:00:29,910 --> 00:00:32,030
In the year 850,

8
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:36,870
the Colossal Titan reappeared
and demolished another wall.

9
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:41,540
Once again, humanity allowed the
Titans to further their advance.

10
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:45,840
One after another, soldiers fell to the Titans.

11
00:00:46,050 --> 00:00:47,380
And then...

12
00:00:47,590 --> 00:00:48,550
Eren!

13
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:50,180
Hurry!

14
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:57,890
Eren Jaeger, who had fallen prey to one...

15
00:01:00,770 --> 00:01:05,690
...reappeared from inside a mysterious Titan.

16
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:10,740
Attention!

17
00:01:10,950 --> 00:01:14,910
Dot Pyxis, the top officer in charge
of the entire southern territory,

18
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:19,460
took notice of Eren Jaeger's
strength while fighting in Titan form

19
00:01:19,670 --> 00:01:23,880
and decided to carry out an unusual plan.

20
00:01:24,090 --> 00:01:27,170
In Titan form,
he will lift that giant rock,

21
00:01:27,380 --> 00:01:31,010
carry it to the wrecked gate,
and seal the hole!

22
00:01:32,050 --> 00:01:34,010
Should this operation succeed,

23
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:39,850
humanity will have taken back land
from the Titans for the very first time!

24
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:43,020
For us, that single, small step...

25
00:01:43,230 --> 00:01:45,400
...will be a great leap forward!

26
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:53,990
However, that plan was on the
verge of failure as soon as it began...

27
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:16,140
Unknown are the names
of the flowers that have been trampled

28
00:02:16,350 --> 00:02:21,600
Birds have fallen to the earth
and long for the wind

29
00:02:21,810 --> 00:02:26,690
Prayers won't solve anything

30
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:32,030
Only the will to fight
can change the here and now!

31
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:37,330
O pigs who laugh at the resolve
to walk over corpses to move forward

32
00:02:37,540 --> 00:02:39,870
Livestock complacency? False prosperity?

33
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:42,750
Give us the freedom of dying,
starving wolves!

34
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:48,130
The humiliation of being caged
is what triggers us to fight back

35
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:53,430
We hunters slaughter prey
beyond the castle walls,

36
00:02:53,630 --> 00:02:58,640
consumed with surging bloodlust,

37
00:02:58,850 --> 00:03:05,770
as our crimson bows and arrows
pierce scarlet holes into the twilight

38
00:03:27,979 --> 00:03:32,984
Wound: The Struggle for Trost, Part 8

39
00:03:35,970 --> 00:03:38,010
We've successfully managed to gather

40
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:41,220
most of the Titans
into the corner of the city,

41
00:03:41,430 --> 00:03:44,140
yet, despite avoiding
combat as much as possible,

42
00:03:44,350 --> 00:03:47,150
around 20% of our soldiers have been lost.

43
00:03:47,770 --> 00:03:50,230
No, they were not "lost."

44
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:53,490
The soldiers did not
die of their own accord.

45
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:58,200
I ordered them to their deaths.

46
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:02,790
Humanity is now perched on
the brink of extinction.

47
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,040
If it means ensuring humankind's survival,

48
00:04:06,250 --> 00:04:09,080
I'm willing to go down
in history as a butcher.

49
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:28,020
Ackermann!

50
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:41,950
Hey! Stop, Ackermann!

51
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,580
Get away from him!

52
00:04:43,790 --> 00:04:46,160
Eren! Don't you recognize me?!

53
00:04:46,370 --> 00:04:47,960
I'm Mikasa!

54
00:04:48,170 --> 00:04:50,580
Part of your family!

55
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:54,510
You have to seal the hole with that rock!

56
00:04:54,710 --> 00:04:56,920
The operation's a failure.

57
00:04:57,130 --> 00:05:01,640
I knew there was no "secret weapon."

58
00:05:06,310 --> 00:05:08,310
Eren! You're human!

59
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:09,650
You're..!

60
00:05:09,850 --> 00:05:11,480
Dodge, Ackermann!

61
00:05:26,290 --> 00:05:28,000
What the hell?!

62
00:05:28,210 --> 00:05:30,040
He's just a regular, dumb Titan!

63
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:32,540
- Eren!
- Captain Ian!

64
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:34,340
Two Titans approaching from ahead!

65
00:05:34,550 --> 00:05:37,010
A 10-meter one and a 6-meter one!

66
00:05:37,210 --> 00:05:41,640
One 12-meter Titan is closing in from the rear!

67
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:45,140
Ian! We have to withdraw!

68
00:05:45,350 --> 00:05:48,350
There's no way that kid's sealing the hole!

69
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:52,520
Agreed. We have no
choice but to leave him here.

70
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:03,030
Red smoke shell from the Elite Squad!

71
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:07,490
It seems the mission to seal
the hole has hit a serious snag.

72
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:09,200
For nothing...!

73
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:12,880
Our friends...
have died for nothing!

74
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:16,670
Hey, look over there!

75
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:19,050
What is it?! What's wrong?!

76
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:22,050
They've... failed?

77
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:23,680
How?

78
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:30,890
Hey! Where are you going, Armin?!

79
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:32,640
Commander Pyxis.

80
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:35,610
We should go back to
defending the gate immediately.

81
00:06:35,810 --> 00:06:36,690
Just give the word, Sir.

82
00:06:36,900 --> 00:06:38,320
No.

83
00:06:38,780 --> 00:06:40,610
Shall I order the
Elite Squad to withdraw?

84
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:41,610
No.

85
00:06:41,820 --> 00:06:46,450
Continue to lure the
Titans into the corner of town.

86
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:50,620
As for the Elite Squad, I've left all
on-site decision-making in their hands.

87
00:06:50,830 --> 00:06:52,920
They're more than just skilled.

88
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:57,500
They're the best of the best, with the
fate of humankind on their shoulders.

89
00:06:57,710 --> 00:07:01,630
Admitting defeat so easily is not an option.

90
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:05,890
If we don't want our fallen
soldiers' deaths to be in vain...

91
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:10,270
...then we must struggle
for as long as we live.

92
00:07:10,470 --> 00:07:13,440
Hey! This is no time
to hesitate! Make the call!

93
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:15,850
Ian! It isn't your fault!

94
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:18,270
This whole mission
was a long shot to begin with!

95
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:19,690
We all understand!

96
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:23,900
It was worth a shot,
and we did the best that we could!

97
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:27,370
So our teams are
going back up the wall now!

98
00:07:29,790 --> 00:07:31,120
Wait!

99
00:07:31,330 --> 00:07:34,210
Wait. Calm down, Ackermann...

100
00:07:34,410 --> 00:07:37,670
Rico Team, take out
the 12-meter one to the rear!

101
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:39,880
Mitabi Team and my team
will deal with the two ahead!

102
00:07:40,090 --> 00:07:40,960
What?!

103
00:07:41,170 --> 00:07:43,380
I was the one put in charge!

104
00:07:43,590 --> 00:07:45,970
Do as you're ordered!

105
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:49,300
We can't leave Jaeger defenseless!

106
00:07:50,180 --> 00:07:51,520
Change of plans!

107
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:55,390
We're to defend Jaeger from the
other Titans until we can recover him!

108
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:58,480
He holds a precious chance for humanity.

109
00:07:58,690 --> 00:08:00,980
We can't abandon him just like that!

110
00:08:01,190 --> 00:08:05,280
Because unlike us, he can't be replaced.

111
00:08:05,490 --> 00:08:07,950
Hundreds of people
have died in this mission alone

112
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:10,740
for that failure of a human weapon!

113
00:08:10,950 --> 00:08:14,660
Yet you want to recover him and go
through this same thing all over again?!

114
00:08:14,870 --> 00:08:15,960
That's right.

115
00:08:16,170 --> 00:08:19,460
We have to keep trying,
no matter how many people die!

116
00:08:26,090 --> 00:08:28,300
What happened with Eren?!

117
00:08:28,510 --> 00:08:30,430
Armin's on his way there.

118
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:32,930
It'll be all right... I think.

119
00:08:33,140 --> 00:08:34,220
You think?

120
00:08:34,430 --> 00:08:36,600
I'm sure everything will be fine.

121
00:08:36,810 --> 00:08:39,610
- Eren'll pull through for us!
- Yeah...

122
00:08:39,810 --> 00:08:42,230
Gathering the Titans in the corner of town

123
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:43,940
seems nothing but pointless to me.

124
00:08:44,150 --> 00:08:47,610
A fight against a Titan always
turns into a battle of attrition.

125
00:08:47,820 --> 00:08:51,200
We need to avoid losing men
at this point in time.

126
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:56,710
Meaning soldiers who die at
"this point in time" are dying for nothing?

127
00:08:56,910 --> 00:08:58,580
We'll wage war someday!

128
00:08:58,790 --> 00:09:02,040
So it makes sense to minimize our
losses and conserve our manpower

129
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:04,050
until that time comes!

130
00:09:04,250 --> 00:09:07,090
- This was the right call to make!
- Was it really, though?

131
00:09:07,300 --> 00:09:09,050
It was!

132
00:09:09,260 --> 00:09:12,510
Well, let's just try not
to end up being "losses."

133
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:14,770
Both of us.

134
00:09:14,970 --> 00:09:16,640
Are you serious, Ian?!

135
00:09:16,850 --> 00:09:19,560
How is humanity ever
going to beat the Titans then?!

136
00:09:19,770 --> 00:09:21,610
Tell me, Rico!

137
00:09:21,810 --> 00:09:24,780
What other way do we have of
putting an end to all this?!

138
00:09:24,980 --> 00:09:27,860
How can we defeat the
overwhelming might of the Titans

139
00:09:28,070 --> 00:09:32,450
while maintaining our humanity
and not letting anyone die?!

140
00:09:32,660 --> 00:09:37,290
I have no idea how to
defeat the Titans, obviously.

141
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:38,620
Yes.

142
00:09:38,830 --> 00:09:42,880
That's why we must do this now.
It's our only option.

143
00:09:43,090 --> 00:09:46,800
We have to lay down
our lives and go down bravely

144
00:09:47,010 --> 00:09:50,760
for this so-called human weapon
we barely know anything about!

145
00:09:51,470 --> 00:09:53,260
It's pathetic, isn't it?

146
00:09:53,470 --> 00:09:57,430
That this is all we humans can do...

147
00:09:57,640 --> 00:10:00,390
So, what do you say?

148
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:03,520
This is our battle to wage.

149
00:10:03,730 --> 00:10:06,400
Our chance to struggle!

150
00:10:16,030 --> 00:10:18,870
I refuse.

151
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:20,580
Rico!

152
00:10:20,790 --> 00:10:22,960
I'll follow your plan.

153
00:10:23,170 --> 00:10:26,550
I think your assessment is right.

154
00:10:26,750 --> 00:10:28,710
I'm going to struggle with all my might

155
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:31,470
and make them taste
the ferocity of humanity.

156
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:34,430
Because I refuse to die for nothing.

157
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:38,520
My team will handle
the 12-meter one to the rear.

158
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:44,310
Let's go! We have the two in front!

159
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:45,940
Yeah.

160
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:50,940
Thank you, Captain Ian.

161
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:54,320
There's no need to thank me, Ackermann.

162
00:10:54,530 --> 00:10:58,580
I was scared stiff there, since there
was no telling what you might do next.

163
00:10:58,790 --> 00:11:00,910
Now you can act freely,
as originally planned.

164
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:03,830
That should make
better use of your ability.

165
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,460
Yes, Sir.

166
00:11:05,670 --> 00:11:08,340
This is to protect your lover, after all.

167
00:11:08,550 --> 00:11:10,170
He's family...

168
00:11:16,220 --> 00:11:17,550
Huh?

169
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:20,560
The damaged parts haven't repaired?

170
00:11:20,770 --> 00:11:23,190
Is it because of his earlier wounds?

171
00:11:24,900 --> 00:11:26,610
How is it affecting Eren?

172
00:11:26,810 --> 00:11:31,900
In fact, what guarantee is there
that he can turn back to normal at all?

173
00:11:32,110 --> 00:11:33,450
No, never mind.

174
00:11:33,650 --> 00:11:36,070
I won't figure anything out just by thinking.

175
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:40,080
For now, I have to do what I can do!

176
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:50,210
Eren... Mikasa...

177
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:52,050
What happened?!

178
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:21,620
Huh?

179
00:12:21,830 --> 00:12:27,540
What... am I doing now?

180
00:12:27,750 --> 00:12:30,090
Am I sitting?

181
00:12:30,290 --> 00:12:32,420
I can't see anything...

182
00:12:32,630 --> 00:12:35,670
What day is today?

183
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:37,380
Where am I?

184
00:12:43,390 --> 00:12:45,270
Oh...

185
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:46,890
I'm home...

186
00:12:54,150 --> 00:12:55,860
I'm gonna sleep.

187
00:13:02,830 --> 00:13:04,240
Eren...

188
00:13:05,750 --> 00:13:08,290
What are you doing, Eren?!

189
00:13:09,460 --> 00:13:10,330
Listen up!

190
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:14,210
We can't let any Titans leave
this corner of town, no matter what!

191
00:13:14,420 --> 00:13:17,920
Focus on that and keep luring them!

192
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:21,760
You don't need to fight them! Is that clear?

193
00:13:21,970 --> 00:13:24,970
You'll run along the ground,
three cadets per team.

194
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:26,980
When you reach the wall,
you leap back up.

195
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:28,690
Don't die out there.

196
00:13:28,890 --> 00:13:32,480
If by some slim chance a
Titan goes astray, we'll take it out.

197
00:13:32,690 --> 00:13:34,110
"By some slim chance?"

198
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:36,610
There's a pretty good chance, if you ask me.

199
00:13:36,820 --> 00:13:38,860
If we sense any risk,

200
00:13:39,070 --> 00:13:41,320
are we free to act on our own discretion?

201
00:13:41,530 --> 00:13:43,950
If it'll help somehow.

202
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:47,580
Kirschtein Team, move out!

203
00:13:47,790 --> 00:13:49,210
Yes, Sir!

204
00:14:07,850 --> 00:14:09,850
Crap! Behind us!

205
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:12,020
One 13-meter Titan!

206
00:14:12,230 --> 00:14:14,360
It's headed straight for Jaeger!

207
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:18,150
We have more Titans
coming through the gate!

208
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:20,570
Four of them, around ten meters high!

209
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:22,990
- Ackermann! You have the rear one!
- Understood!

210
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:25,740
Don't let it get to Jaeger!

211
00:14:25,950 --> 00:14:28,370
- Let's hold 'em off here!
- Understood!

212
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:32,170
Elite soldiers or not, two teams
can't handle four Titans at once...

213
00:14:47,390 --> 00:14:48,770
This can't be...

214
00:14:48,970 --> 00:14:51,390
Why are there so many Titans

215
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:53,850
even though there are so few people here?

216
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:57,360
Wait, could it be that Eren
is drawing them in?!

217
00:14:57,570 --> 00:14:58,980
Mikasa!

218
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:00,440
What happened to the plan?!

219
00:15:00,650 --> 00:15:01,650
Armin!

220
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:03,780
What's happened to Eren?!

221
00:15:03,990 --> 00:15:05,410
Get away! It's dangerous there!

222
00:15:05,620 --> 00:15:08,740
That Titan isn't acting through Eren's will!

223
00:15:08,950 --> 00:15:11,290
I called out to him,
but he wouldn't respond!

224
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:13,330
There's no getting through to him anymore!

225
00:15:13,540 --> 00:15:14,420
What about the plan?!

226
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:16,000
It's failed!

227
00:15:16,210 --> 00:15:19,090
We're fighting because
we can't leave Eren behind!

228
00:15:19,300 --> 00:15:21,210
But there are too many Titans...

229
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:24,260
At this rate,
we'll eventually be wiped out!

230
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:37,810
From the back of the
head to the nape of the neck...

231
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:41,480
...one meter high and ten centimeters across!

232
00:15:41,690 --> 00:15:42,610
Armin!

233
00:15:42,820 --> 00:15:44,780
I'll get Eren out of here!

234
00:15:44,990 --> 00:15:47,450
You just protect us from the other Titans!

235
00:15:47,660 --> 00:15:50,620
Huh? What are you...?

236
00:15:50,830 --> 00:15:54,460
Eren came out of the Titans' vital spot!

237
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:58,250
My guess is that has something to do

238
00:15:58,460 --> 00:16:00,750
with whatever makes the Titans tick.

239
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,130
It's okay...

240
00:16:02,340 --> 00:16:04,380
As long as I miss the center...

241
00:16:05,380 --> 00:16:07,180
...he won't die.

242
00:16:07,390 --> 00:16:10,390
It'll just...

243
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:11,770
...hurt a little bit!

244
00:16:11,970 --> 00:16:13,390
Armin!

245
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:24,690
Stop, Armin! That's too reckless!

246
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:25,700
Mikasa!

247
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:30,490
Just go do what you can!
There are lives you can help save!

248
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:33,370
Leave Eren to me and go!

249
00:16:40,420 --> 00:16:42,670
Eren! Can you hear me?!

250
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:44,420
Pull yourself together!

251
00:16:44,630 --> 00:16:47,510
We're all going to die
if you don't come out of there!

252
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:50,010
Don't give in to the Titan's body!

253
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:54,680
Now just hurry and
get out of this lump of flesh!

254
00:16:54,890 --> 00:16:57,350
Get out of here?

255
00:16:57,560 --> 00:16:59,270
Why?

256
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:02,020
I'm sleepy now...

257
00:17:02,230 --> 00:17:03,440
Eren!

258
00:17:03,650 --> 00:17:05,780
Come out! Hurry!

259
00:17:05,990 --> 00:17:08,200
Eren! Eren!

260
00:17:12,780 --> 00:17:15,700
What happened to avenging your mother?!

261
00:17:15,910 --> 00:17:18,210
You were gonna drive
out all the Titans, remember?!

262
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:22,540
You hate them for killing
your mother, remember?!

263
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:26,340
What are you talking about, Armin?

264
00:17:26,550 --> 00:17:30,010
My mom's right here...

265
00:17:30,220 --> 00:17:31,800
Eren! Eren!

266
00:17:32,010 --> 00:17:33,970
Wake up, Eren!

267
00:17:34,180 --> 00:17:36,390
You're in there, aren't you?! Eren!

268
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:39,850
If we stay here, the Titans will kill us!

269
00:17:40,060 --> 00:17:41,980
It'll all end here!

270
00:17:43,770 --> 00:17:48,450
Seriously, you're not making any sense, Armin...

271
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:53,530
Why should I have to go outside?

272
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:55,490
Yeah...

273
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:58,370
Why would I want to leave?

274
00:18:01,670 --> 00:18:04,380
Why would I want to join the Scouts...?

275
00:18:13,260 --> 00:18:16,640
Like it or not, we're on our own now!

276
00:18:27,070 --> 00:18:28,490
Go'! you!

277
00:18:34,740 --> 00:18:37,660
About time you kicked the bucket, bastard!

278
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,130
Make distance for now!

279
00:18:44,330 --> 00:18:45,960
I've returned!

280
00:18:46,170 --> 00:18:48,300
I'll rendezvous with Mitabi Team!

281
00:18:58,100 --> 00:18:59,520
Huh?!

282
00:19:05,020 --> 00:19:05,810
Jean!

283
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:07,440
Get going!

284
00:19:11,110 --> 00:19:14,280
I've had enough of
people dying because of me!

285
00:19:29,420 --> 00:19:31,970
Damn! Of all the times to have a malfunction!

286
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:51,860
Jean!

287
00:19:56,740 --> 00:19:58,410
What's going on?

288
00:19:58,620 --> 00:20:00,950
Why isn't he using his ODM gear?!

289
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:03,290
Oh no!

290
00:20:03,500 --> 00:20:05,460
Don't tell me it's malfunctioning?!

291
00:20:06,420 --> 00:20:08,330
I'll manage somehow!

292
00:20:19,930 --> 00:20:24,230
Damn... I can't believe
I'm draggin' everyone down...

293
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:40,780
Will this really work out somehow?

294
00:20:43,660 --> 00:20:44,870
Eren...

295
00:20:45,540 --> 00:20:46,960
Eren...

296
00:20:47,420 --> 00:20:48,630
Eren...

297
00:20:50,340 --> 00:20:51,750
Eren...

298
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:57,930
We're supposed to explore the
outside world someday, remember?

299
00:21:00,260 --> 00:21:03,930
Far beyond these walls, there stretch

300
00:21:04,140 --> 00:21:10,940
fiery waters, lands of ice,
and sandy snowfields...

301
00:21:11,150 --> 00:21:14,980
The world my mom and
dad planned to venture into.

302
00:21:19,610 --> 00:21:22,450
I figured you'd just forgotten,

303
00:21:22,660 --> 00:21:24,740
but you actually stopped talking about it

304
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:29,170
because you didn't want
me to join the Scouts, huh?

305
00:21:29,370 --> 00:21:32,210
The outside... world...?

306
00:21:35,630 --> 00:21:38,420
Eren... Answer me...

307
00:21:38,630 --> 00:21:43,510
Even though just one step
outside the wall lies a hellish world...

308
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:48,770
And even though it might mean
dying a gruesome death like my parents...

309
00:21:48,980 --> 00:21:54,020
Why did you want to
venture into the outside world?!

310
00:21:56,650 --> 00:21:58,070
Why?

311
00:21:59,530 --> 00:22:02,620
Isn't that obvious?

312
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:06,490
Because...

313
00:22:06,700 --> 00:22:09,080
...I was born in this world!

314
00:22:36,520 --> 00:22:41,450
Your dreams are where your heart is

315
00:22:41,650 --> 00:22:47,700
They're more fragile than life itself

316
00:22:47,910 --> 00:22:52,370
Over and over you cast them aside,
only to find more

317
00:22:52,580 --> 00:22:59,050
Now, rest in peace

318
00:22:59,260 --> 00:23:10,390
Pounding impulses defile the things we wish for

319
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:20,650
and the more we forget
the more we remember again

320
00:23:20,860 --> 00:23:26,620
In this beautiful, cruel world

321
00:23:26,820 --> 00:23:31,790
all I can do is ask why we're still alive

322
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:37,500
Oh, with our strength... and our weakness...

323
00:23:37,710 --> 00:23:43,170
what are we going to protect if there's no sense

324
00:23:43,380 --> 00:23:46,800
to anything anymore?

325
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:56,900
Go! Run! Live!

326
00:23:57,110 --> 00:24:02,150
As innumerable words mix and
countless lives are lost on the battlefield,

327
00:24:02,360 --> 00:24:05,382
Eren holds hope aloft and heads for the gate.

328
00:24:05,382 --> 00:24:06,780
Primal Desire: The Struggle for Trost, Part 9
Eren holds hope aloft and heads for the gate.

329
00:24:06,780 --> 00:24:06,966
Primal Desire: The Struggle for Trost, Part 9
